        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
                <heading>Lifting Model</heading>
                <p class="text-justify">
                    We modify <a href="https://guytevet.github.io/mdm-page/" style="font-size: 14px;">MDM</a> to condition on a sequence of 2D hand keypoints \& camera parameters. The conditioning module combines different input representations: 3D pose (rotation, translation) of camera, <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.14817" style="font-size: 14px;">Plucker rays</a> & <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2312.06594" style="font-size: 14px;">KPE</a>.
                </p>
                <div style="margin-top:20px"></div>
                <a href="assets/lifting.png"><center><img style="width:100%;max-width:100%" src="assets/lifting.png"></center></a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top:20px"></div>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
                <heading>Forecasting Model</heading>
                <p class="text-justify">
                    We modify <a href="https://guytevet.github.io/mdm-page/" style="font-size: 14px;">MDM</a> to condition on images features extracted from a ViT backbone. Each input & output token is 198-dimensional: 2 hands x (16 (joints) x (6 (6D rotation for each joint) + 3 (wrist translation))).
                </p>
                <div style="margin-top:20px"></div>
                <a href="assets/forecasting.png"><center><img style="width:100%;max-width:100%" src="assets/forecasting.png"></center></a>
            </div>
        </div>

